hate content during the cell cycle of human leukemic (HL-60) cells</article-title><source>J Cell Physiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10362021</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sweet</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Singh G: Accumulation of human promyelocytic leukemic (HL-60) cells at two energetic cell cycle checkpoints</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1995</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>5164</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7585566</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorward</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sweet</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Moorehead</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mitochondrial contributions to cancer cell physiology: Redox balance, cell cycle and drug resistance</article-title><source>J Bioenerg Biomembr</source><year>1997</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9387099</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldenthal</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Marin-Garcia</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mitochondrial signaling pathways: A receiver/integrator organelle</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biochem</source><year>2004</year><volume>262</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15532704</pub-id></element-citation>